        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Fix broken links. I've received general feedback that using wayback machine is the right way to go.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Generally, I use the latest version that's available, including redirects. In a few cases, there's no such page on wayback machine either, and I have to remove the link. In a few other places there are better places to link to.</p>",
