        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/576623?u=88392c52422628facfd7cf108241d2864680915d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add interactive examples to <code class=\"notranslate\">sin()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">cos()</code> CSS functions.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On September 2025, both <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/sin\" rel=\"nofollow\">sin()</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/cos\" rel=\"nofollow\">cos()</a> will become <a href=\"https://web.dev/baseline\" rel=\"nofollow\">baseline widely available</a>, yet both MDN articles have minimal information about the functions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The interactive examples interface enhances the learning experience by allowing visitors to modify the code and see the results. This is a more instructive way to understand how these CSS functions work.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1324227543\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/19016\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/19016/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/19016\">#19016</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1327573895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/19119\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/19119/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/19119\">#19119</a></li>\n</ul>",
